Chapter: SensorsStub
  cites Foreword chapter Sensors

 The Sensors effect, answered by constants, because this machine has no
 accelerometer, no gyroscope, no barometer and no light sensor.

 Same arrangement as Foreword chapter LocationStub and for the same
 reason: an unimplemented effect operation dies at emit with CDX2040, so
 a program that mentions a sensor cannot be built even if it never
 performs the read. Constants let that program be written and tested now.
 sensors-are-fixed answers False and is the question a caller asks before
 believing anything below.

 The values are chosen to be recognisable rather than plausible, which is
 the opposite of what a convincing fake would do.

 A device lying still on a table reads zero on two accelerometer axes and
 one gravity on the third, so that is what is here: z reads one whole g
 and nothing else moves. It is the textbook at-rest reading, which means
 a caller that treats it as live data gets the one answer that is
 obviously the default. Gyroscope is zero on every axis -- not rotating.
 Barometer is standard sea-level pressure exactly, 101325 pascals, a
 defined constant rather than a measurement. Light level is zero lux:
 dark, and no camera shutter should ever be chosen from it.

 We say:

Section: Units

 Acceleration is milli-g, so one gravity is a thousand. Rotation is
 milli-degrees per second. Pressure is pascals. Illuminance is lux.

  sensors-milli-g-per-g : Integer = 1000

Section: The Fixed Answers

  SensorAxes = record {
    sx-x : Integer,
    sx-y : Integer,
    sx-z : Integer
  }

  sensors-stub-barometer : Integer = 101325
  sensors-stub-light-level : Integer = 0

  sensors-are-fixed : [Sensors] Boolean
  sensors-are-fixed = False

  accelerometer : [Sensors] SensorAxes
  accelerometer = SensorAxes { sx-x = 0, sx-y = 0, sx-z = sensors-milli-g-per-g }

  gyroscope : [Sensors] SensorAxes
  gyroscope = SensorAxes { sx-x = 0, sx-y = 0, sx-z = 0 }

  barometer : [Sensors] Integer
  barometer = sensors-stub-barometer

  light-level : [Sensors] Integer
  light-level = sensors-stub-light-level

